@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+# Sileo recorder surface
+
+Vendored from **hiaaryan/sileo 0.1.6**, MIT, commit
+`b70fd826537dcdf0329e55f1e9ab208a66b61c79`, `packages/sileo/src/`.
+https://github.com/hiaaryan/sileo/tree/b70fd826537dcdf0329e55f1e9ab208a66b61c79/packages/sileo
+
+The recorder uses the actual `Sileo` component, not a native drawing of it.
+The two SVG rectangles, Gaussian blur/alpha-threshold/composite filter, 600 ms
+spring with 0.25 bounce, header morph, measurement and content fade are upstream.
+
+Local changes to `sileo.tsx`: controlled expansion for touch; responsive width;
+a `bounce` prop (the recorder uses 0 so the body expands once without
+overshooting); pre-measured expanded SVG height; toast container height,
+horizontal body footprint (`x`/`width`), and clipped bottom content container
+(`height`/`clipPath`) locked to the same body spring so expand and minimize are
+symmetric without clipping or horizontal bar overhang; `useReducedMotion` for SVG
+targets; a group root and an actual header button so interactive recorder
+controls are not nested in a button; hidden content is inert. Toast-only
+hover/swipe/refresh code remains upstream but is not attached to the recorder
+root. `styles.css`, constants, icons and types are unchanged.
+Application-specific styling is in `../RecorderSetup.css`.
+
+The separate `recorder.html` entry loads only React, Motion, this surface and
+the shared Record button. It does not initialize the editor, Pixi, or HeroUI.
+Android owns the small transparent setup window; it is removed before capture.
+
+MIT license notice: see `LICENSE`.
